## Practical 3 — Map-Based Visualization: Steps Only

1. Open Tableau and connect to `Superstore.csv`.
2. Create a new worksheet.
3. Find State in the Data pane.
4. Double-click State to generate the map.
5. Right-click State → Geographic Role → State/Province.
6. Drag Country to Filters.
7. Select United States and click OK.
8. Ensure the Marks type is Map.
9. Drag Profit to Color on the Marks card.
10. Click Color → Edit Colors → choose a green palette → OK.
11. Drag State to Label.
12. Drag Profit to Label.
13. Ensure the aggregation is `SUM(Profit)`.
14. Double-click the worksheet title and enter Profit By States.
15. Check that the USA map displays state names, profit values, and green shading.
16. Save the workbook.
